. This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\n## Change\n- Switch `quantize` rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (and update the import).\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 409123, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0145ZH2AYm5qMEfMPqwcSYhG", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 409123, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0145ZH2AYm5qMEfMPqwcSYhG", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 411458, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01NJPeRQqvK87hbF77c2QSQB", "tool": "request_review", "args": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 411758, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01NJPeRQqvK87hbF77c2QSQB", "tool": "request_review", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 411758, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01NJPeRQqvK87hbF77c2QSQB", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 415736, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py`'s own description says it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212), but the code used standard round-half-up. So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of `2.66`, which made `tests/test_money.py` fail.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` and updated the import (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. When it first opened, alex wasn't listed as a reviewer, so I added him separately. He's now on the PR.\n\nFIN-212 isn't in the security advisory system, so I relied on the code and test, which agree on banker's rounding. I didn't merge the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RPpxjbuWgZHaKorQcrbnG9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014h9gLboa9TCtYqqScrKTnF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018ogBgweYu8jf5gH7dh6WNi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212", "confidence": 0.8}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01PeK6oRPqX85G9qwagEpdw5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012mJHsiRAUtSYvggeUEpzma", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Mp84BcpgoGEXxcWh1wBRDk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TVoqYRatoFxWqdUwc3PYcm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the commit. Opening the PR now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0145ZH2AYm5qMEfMPqwcSYhG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\n`round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\n## Change\n- Switch `quantize` rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (and update the import).\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR opened, but the response shows no reviewers attached. I'll request alex directly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NJPeRQqvK87hbF77c2QSQB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py`'s own description says it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212), but the code used standard round-half-up. So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of `2.66`, which made `tests/test_money.py` fail.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` and updated the import (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. When it first opened, alex wasn't listed as a reviewer, so I added him separately. He's now on the PR.\n\nFIN-212 isn't in the security advisory system, so I relied on the code and test, which agree on banker's rounding. I didn't merge the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}